          <div class="views-row">
      <div class="views-field views-field-rendered-entity"><span class="field-content">    
<div class="node--embedded">
    <h2>
        <a href="/code/28/09" rel="bookmark"><span class="field field--name-title field--type-string field--label-hidden">Chapter 28.09  Mechanical Installations</span>
</a>
    </h2>
    



<div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--label-hidden field--name-field-prefix-note field--type-text-long ck-content"><div class="field__item"><p>(Amended by Ordinances 181437, <a href="https://efiles.portlandoregon.gov/record/15844599">191154</a>, and <a href="https://efiles.portlandoregon.gov/record/17150613">192002</a>, effective January 10, 2025.)</p><p><span>All mechanical work, including but not limited to heating, air conditioning, ventilating, gas piping and woodstoves, must be designed and installed in accordance with the&nbsp;Oregon Mechanical Specialty Code, any other relevant Specialty Codes, Title 27 and this Chapter.&nbsp;Permits and inspections will be required for all work except as specifically exempted by this Title.</span></p><p><span>Existing mechanical work that was lawfully in place in Portland on January 1, 2008, or that was constructed or relocated under a valid permit after that date, will be considered an existing nonconforming condition as provided in this Title.</span></p></div></div><div class="views-element-container">
<div class="mb-6 view view-eva view-city-code-list view-id-city_code_list view-display-id-eva_embedded_code_chapters js-view-dom-id-ed1641539a1b9c9ada88e773b3727c10d6c4b83a02ce47aa0316b6ecb8786a7a">
  
    

  
  

  
  
  

  
  

  
  </div>
</div>
<div class="views-element-container">
<div class="mb-6 view view-eva view-city-code-list view-id-city_code_list view-display-id-eva_embedded_code_sections js-view-dom-id-298dc3fc5dc07563da0059e3be543e02b0c32f8af2b3c52f9552b943cda3e8d7">
  
    

  
  

  
  
  

  
  

  
  </div>
</div>

</div>
</span></div>
    </div>
  
    </div>
  
          </div>
</div>

    </div>
  </div>

    </div>
  
